meta {
  name: 09 Bad status filter — does it 400 cleanly?
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/agent-listings/mine?status=PURGATORY
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  status: PURGATORY
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: gte 400
  res.status: lt 500
}

docs {
  Defensive probe. If a typo on the client side silently returns "all
  assignments" instead of an error, that's the kind of bug that hides in
  production for months.

  Expected: 400 with a clear "PURGATORY is not a valid status" detail. A
  200 with everything would be a meaningful problem.
}
